# Worker reasoning effort (Chase lock 2026-08-24)

When launching Opus / Fable / Grok via `claude-human-stream` /
`agent-human-stream`, pass `--effort` from the **job lane**, not vibes.

| Lane | Opus | Fable | Grok |
|------|------|-------|------|
| **Code** (implement, PR, land, deploy, RCA that edits) | `medium` | `high` | `xhigh` |
| **Research** (조사, open-source scan, no code change) | `low` | `low` | `medium` |

**Default research owner is Grok.** Opus/Fable research only when Chase
names them — still `low`.

Claude Code CLI enum is `low|medium|high|xhigh|max` (Fable / Opus 4.7+).
When Chase names **max** or **xhigh**, pass that string —
**do not** remap Fable `max` → `high`. Wrapper aliases: `maximum` → `max`,
`mid` → `medium`, `x-high` → `xhigh`.

Grok CLI enum is `xhigh|high|medium|low` (no `max` / `mid`). The wrapper
maps `mid` → `medium` and `max`/`maximum` → `xhigh` (Grok ceiling).

Wrapper default when `--effort` is omitted = **code lane**
(Opus `medium`, Fable `high`, Grok `xhigh`). Named `max` is not that
default. Research launches **must** pass `--effort` (`medium` for Grok,
`low` for Opus/Fable). Mixed research-then-implement in one worker →
code lane.

SoT: `~/.agents/skills/sume-main-agent-orchestration/SKILL.md`
§ "Worker reasoning effort".
